  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLICK-Improve access to agricultural biz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting agribusiness for families of farmers with disabilities to generate sustainable income for families and people with physical disabilities in the agricultural profession.

Many persons with disabilities have limited career opportunities - creating jobs where they do not have a core and stable job. In addition, the families of the physically challenged have to concentrate on the energy, time, and expenses of their daily family life. And also see that they still lack the capital to own a stable and have a sustainable income in life.

Farming is considered as a way to help them and their families financially secure without having to travel long distances to work in other areas, they can do business in their own area and their family can help them in their career.

This program will be successful because we have taken into account the potential and needs of the beneficiaries and believe that doing businessin agriculture will help them succeed and create a career for them. And this plan will becarefully monitored and consulted by an experienced program team.

Helping people with disabilities and their families build sustainable careers through capacity building, business planning, income-expenditure, and business start-ups for people with disabilities and their families can help them earn a better living and a better income.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="72">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLICK Information for Development</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLICK is a local non-profit organization established since 2007 for promoting freedom of information and freedom of expression for development. Main activities include facilitating online repositories and discussion groups, community learning center, information clubs at colleges, social media, documentation of good practices, facilitation and documentation of learning events, media productions and networking of organizations.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
